  "body": " Rates of Work       Strand  1.0 Numbers and Algebra    Sub-Strand  1.2 Compound Proportions, Rates of Work and Mixtures    Specific Learning Outcomes  Compute rates of work from real life situations          A rate of work is a compound proportion: the work done depends on how many work, how fast each works, and for how long. In this section we measure work as a fraction of the whole job, so that people and machines working at different speeds can be combined.   Why does it matter how fast people and machines work?      Working Together   Filling the Bucket   Learners fill a bucket from a drum, one cup at a time. Each learner has a cup of the same size and works at the same speed.     One learner takes seconds, two take seconds and three take seconds. Predict the time for four learners, then check it.    Asha alone fills the bucket in seconds and Brian alone in seconds. What fraction of the bucket does each fill in one second?    What fraction do they fill together in one second? How long do they take together?    Why is the answer not seconds, the mean of their times?        Rate of Work  A job that takes days is done at a rate of work of of the job a day. When people or machines work together, their rates add. The time together is (the combined rate), and the fraction done in days is (the rate). Add the fractions done in one day, not the times.    Two taps and an outlet on a tank. Set the taps with the sliders and watch the tank fill.     Two Welders   Mutua can make a gate in days and Njeri can make one in days. How long do they take working together?    In one day Mutua makes of the gate and Njeri . Together: of the gate a day.  The time is days.     Two Tractors   Tractor A ploughs a farm in hours and tractor B in hours. How long do they take together, and what fraction of the farm do they plough in hours?    Together: of the farm an hour, so hours.  In hours they plough of the farm.     One Starts Early   Kiprop can paint a hall in days and Auma in days. Kiprop works alone for days, then Auma joins and they finish together. How many days does the whole job take?    In days Kiprop paints of the hall, so is left.  Together they paint a day, so the rest takes days. The whole job takes days.    Type numbers only, without Ksh, units, spaces or commas, for example 45326 . Give a fraction as a fraction, for example 7\/12 , or as a decimal correct to 3 decimal places. Give times, masses and volumes exactly or correct to 1 decimal place, and money to the nearest shilling, unless the question says otherwise.                A can do a job in hours and B in hours. How long do they take together?  hours  an hour, so hours.    Two road crews take days and days to do a job alone. How long do they take together, and what fraction of the job do they do in days?  days;    Three workers take , and days to do a job alone. How long do they take together?  days  a day, so days.    Together A and B take days to do a job. A alone takes days. How long does B take alone?  days  B's rate is of the job a day.    A can do a job in days and B in days. A works alone for days, then they finish together. How many days does the job take in all?  days  A does , leaving . Together they do a day, so more days: in all.    Challenge: Twice as Fast  Two workers together take days to do a job. One works twice as fast as the other. How long would each take alone?  If the slower worker does of the job a day, the faster does .  days and days  , so . The slower takes days and the faster days.       Filling, Emptying and Safe Working Hours   Safe Hours on a Long Journey   A bus company runs buses from Nairobi to Mombasa, about , at an average speed of . The company's own rule is that a driver drives at most hours without a -minute rest, at most hours a day, and on at most days a week.     How long is the driving time from Nairobi to Mombasa?    With one rest after hours, how long does the journey take?    The company runs one-way trips a day. How many hours of driving is that a day, and how many drivers are needed each day?    Drivers work days a week, but the buses run every day. How many drivers does the company need?    Why do companies and the law limit how long drivers may drive?        Filling and Emptying  An inlet that fills a tank in hours adds of the tank each hour; an outlet that empties it in hours removes . With both open the net rate is of the tank an hour, and the time to fill is (net rate). If the outlet is faster, the net rate is negative and the tank empties; if they are equally fast, the level never changes. The outlet takes away its fraction each hour.    Safe Working Hours  Tired drivers cause many road crashes. In Kenya the law, and the National Transport and Safety Authority (NTSA), set rules on how long drivers of public service vehicles may drive; look up the current rules. The hours in this chapter are a company's own rules, invented for practice. Keeping to safe hours is part of a driver's responsibility to passengers and other road users.    A School Water Tank   A pump fills the school's water tank in hours. The kitchen taps empty the full tank in hours. The tank is empty and both are turned on. How long does the tank take to fill?    The net rate is of the tank an hour.  The time is hours, that is h min. Check with : set , clear tap B, open the outlet and set .     Two Inlets and a Drain   Two inlets fill a tank in hours and hours, and a drain empties it in hours. With all three open, how long does the empty tank take to fill?    of the tank an hour.  The time is hours (about h min).     How Many Drivers?   A transport company needs hours of driving a week. Its rule is at most hours a day on at most days a week. How many drivers does it need? How many if the daily limit falls to hours?    One driver may drive hours a week. ; drivers give only hours, so drivers are needed.  At hours a day one driver gives hours. , so drivers.    Type numbers only, without Ksh, units, spaces or commas, for example 45326 . Give a fraction as a fraction, for example 7\/12 , or as a decimal correct to 3 decimal places. Give times, masses and volumes exactly or correct to 1 decimal place, and money to the nearest shilling, unless the question says otherwise.            An inlet fills a tank in hours and an outlet empties it in hours. Both are opened when the tank is empty. How long does it take to fill?  hours  an hour.    A tank is full. Its inlet fills it in hours and its outlet empties it in hours. With both open, how long does it take to empty?  hours  It loses of the tank an hour.    A tank is half full. The inlet fills an empty tank in hours and the outlet empties a full one in hours. With both open, how long does it take to fill?  hours  Net rate , and .    A company needs hours of driving a week. Its drivers may drive at most hours a day on days a week. How many drivers does it need?  drivers  ; drivers give only hours, so .    A lorry trip needs hours of driving, and one driver may drive at most hours a day. (a) How many days does the trip take with one driver? (b) How many hours does each drive if two drivers share the driving equally?  (a) days (b) hours each, so the trip can be done in one day    Challenge: A Formula for the Time  Show that an inlet that fills a tank in hours and an outlet that empties it in hours fill the empty tank in hours, when . What happens when ?  The net rate is ; if the tank never fills (the net rate is or negative).  , so the time is . If the net rate is and the level stays where it is; if the outlet is faster and the net rate is negative: the tank never fills.     "
