  "title": "Magnitude of a Vector",
  "body": " Magnitude of a Vector       Strand  2.0 Measurements and Geometry    Sub-Strand  2.2 Vectors    Specific Learning Outcomes  Determine the magnitude of a vector using cartesian coordinates          Measure, Then Calculate      Draw , and with square for . Measure the length of each arrow.    Each arrow, with its across move and its up move, makes a right-angled triangle. Use Pythagoras' theorem to calculate each length.    Does the minus sign in change the length?    Mark and . Write and find its length.        Magnitude  The magnitude of a vector (also called its modulus) is its length. It is written . By Pythagoras on the across and up moves,   The distance between points and is . A multiple has magnitude .    The vector and its components.   The vector (4, −7) with a dashed 4 across and 7 down making a right angle; the vector's length is √65.      Drag the tip of the vector. The dashed lines are its components; Pythagoras gives its length.     Magnitude in a Spreadsheet  Put the -components in column A and the -components in column B, starting in row . In cell C2 type =SQRT(A2^2+B2^2) and copy it down the column: each row gives the magnitude of one vector.    Magnitude from Components   Find the magnitudes of and ( ).        Distance Between Two Places   On a map with unit to , a borehole is at and a water point at . How far is the water point from the borehole in a straight line?    End minus start: .  .     How Far from the Start?   (a) A learner walks east and then north. How far is she from the start?  (b) The boda boda rider in finished at km from the stage after riding . How far is the rider from the stage in a straight line?    (a) Her displacement is , so the distance is .  (b) , much less than the ridden.    Type one number in each box of a column vector: the top box is the move across, the bottom box the move up. Use a minus sign for left or down, for example -3 . Type a square root as sqrt(73) , or give the decimal to 2 decimal places.               Vectors in everyday life: a phone's map shows both the distance by road and the straight-line distance to a place. Which one is the magnitude of a displacement?    Find the magnitude of each vector: , , , .  ; ; ;    Find the distance for and , and the distance for and .  ;    For the matatu in , find the straight-line distance from the start to the finish. Compare it with the driven.  , less than half the distance driven.    Two learners push a handcart with forces N and N. Find the resultant force and its size. Why is the size not N?  N, of size N. The pushes are at right angles, so their sizes do not simply add.    The vector has magnitude . What can be? Give both values.  or  , so and or .    Challenge: Magnitudes of Multiples  . Without using Pythagoras, find and .  Write each vector as a multiple of .  ;  , so its magnitude is . , so its magnitude is .    "
