  "number": "7.1.1.3",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  Say whether each is a great circle, a small circle or half of a great circle.  The parallel of latitude .  The Greenwich meridian.  The Greenwich meridian together with the meridian.  The parallel of latitude .  A circle on the earth's surface of radius .     (a) small; (b) half of a great circle; (c) great; (d) great (it is the equator); (e) small  A great circle has its centre at the centre of the earth. (a) A parallel other than the equator has its centre on the axis above or below the earth's centre: small. (b) A meridian runs from pole to pole only: half of a great circle. (c) The two meridians together make a whole circle through both poles: great. (d) The equator: great. (e) A great circle has radius ; is less, so small.  "
