  "number": "8.2",
  "title": "Compound Interest",
  "body": " Compound Interest       Strand  2.0 Measurements and Geometry    Sub-Strand  2.4 Commercial Arithmetic III    Specific Learning Outcomes  Determine compound interest using the formula           Compound Interest Year by Year and by Formula   Leaving the Interest In   Neema puts Ksh in a bank savings account that pays per annum compound interest. At the end of each year the interest is added to the account.   Neema's Savings Account   Year Balance at the start (Ksh) Interest (Ksh) Balance at the end (Ksh)  1  2  3  4       Complete the table for years.    What single number multiplies the balance each year?    Check your last balance by working out .    How much would Neema have after years at per annum simple interest? How much more does compound interest give?        Compound Interest  With compound interest , the interest is added to the account at the end of each year, and next year's interest is paid on the bigger sum. Each year the amount is multiplied by the same multiplier , , so after whole years where is the principal and the rate per cent per annum. The compound interest is .  The in and the here are the same thing, the rate per cent per annum; we keep the letters in common use.    A Fixed Deposit for Three Years   Ksh is put in a fixed deposit at per annum compound interest for years. Find the amount and the compound interest, to the nearest shilling.    The multiplier is . The amount is Ksh to the nearest shilling, and the compound interest is , Ksh .     Year by Year   Ksh is saved at per annum compound interest. Make a table of the amount at the end of each year for years, and check the last value by the formula.    Each year, multiply by , keeping cents.   Ksh at 4% per annum   End of year Amount (Ksh)  1  2  3    Check: .     Interest in the Third Year   For the account in , how much interest is earned in the third year alone?    , so Ksh . This is of , the balance at the start of the third year; it is more than the earned in the first year.    Type amounts as plain numbers, without Ksh, spaces or commas, for example 45326 . Give money to the nearest shilling and percentages to 1 decimal place unless the question says otherwise; exact answers in cents are also accepted.        Find the amount and the compound interest on Ksh at per annum for years.  Amount Ksh ; compound interest Ksh    Find the amount and the compound interest on Ksh at per annum for years.  Amount Ksh ; compound interest Ksh    A SACCO member leaves Ksh in a fixed deposit at per annum compound interest for years. Find the amount and the interest, to the nearest shilling.  Amount Ksh ; interest Ksh  , so Ksh . The interest is .    A chama deposits Ksh at per annum compound interest. Make a year-by-year table for years and find the interest earned in the third year.  Amounts , , ; interest in the third year Ksh  Multiply by each year: , , . The third year's interest is .    Challenge: Two Years as One  Interest is per annum compound. What single percentage increase is the same as two years of this interest?  Square the multiplier.  (not )  , an increase of , about . It is more than because the second year's interest is also paid on the first year's interest.       Simple and Compound Interest Compared   Watching the Gap Grow   Ksh is saved for years at per annum. Use or a calculator.     Find the amount after years with simple interest and with compound interest.    Find the gap between the two amounts after , , and years.    Why is there no gap after one year?    Move the rate slider to . Does compound interest still pull ahead?        Which Grows Faster?  With simple interest the amount grows by the same number of shillings every year, so its graph against time is a straight line. With compound interest the amount is multiplied by the same number every year, so its graph is a curve that gets steeper. At the same rate the two are equal after one year; after that compound interest is always ahead, and the gap keeps growing.    Simple and compound interest on the same savings. The dashed line is simple interest and the solid curve is compound interest.     SACCO or Bank?   Mumbi has Ksh to save. Her SACCO offers per annum simple interest; a bank offers per annum compound interest. Which is better over years, over years and over years?    The SACCO adds a year; the bank multiplies by a year.   Amounts in Ksh   Years SACCO, simple Bank, compound Better  2 SACCO  3 bank, by  6 bank    Over years the SACCO's higher rate wins. From years on, the bank's compound interest is ahead, and the gap grows.     How Many Years?   A chama saves Ksh at per annum compound interest. After how many whole years is the amount first more than Ksh ?    Try values of in : The amount passes Ksh during the sixth year, so it is first more than Ksh after whole years.    Type amounts as plain numbers, without Ksh, spaces or commas, for example 45326 . Give money to the nearest shilling and percentages to 1 decimal place unless the question says otherwise; exact answers in cents are also accepted.            Ksh is saved for years at per annum. Find the amount at simple interest and at compound interest, and the difference, to the nearest shilling.  Simple Ksh ; compound Ksh ; difference Ksh    Ksh can be saved at per annum simple interest or at per annum compound interest. Which is better over years, and which over years?  years: against , simple. years: against , compound.    Ksh for years: is per annum simple interest or per annum compound interest better?  Compound, by about Ksh ( against )    At per annum compound interest, after how many whole years has money first doubled?  years  , just short of ; . So the money has first doubled after years, whatever the principal.    Ksh is saved at per annum compound interest. After how many whole years is it first more than Ksh ?  years  After years: . After years: .    Challenge: Why the Gap Starts in Year Two  Explain why simple and compound interest at the same rate give the same amount after year, and show that after years compound interest is ahead by exactly .  Expand .  Both pay in year 1. In year 2 compound interest also pays on the first year's interest.  After one year both amounts are . After two years, compound gives and simple gives . The difference is : the interest, at , on the first year's interest .     "
