  "body": " Changing Every Value     A thermometer at a school weather station in Nyeri read too low every day. Its readings had mean and standard deviation . Find the mean and standard deviation of the corrected temperatures.  A test was marked out of ; the marks had mean and standard deviation . The marks are changed to percentages by multiplying by . Find the new mean and standard deviation.      (a) Adding to every reading moves the mean up by but does not change the spread: mean , standard deviation .  (b) Multiplying every mark by multiplies the mean and every distance from the mean by : mean , standard deviation .  In general, if every value becomes with , the mean becomes and the standard deviation becomes .   "
